 aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M7 7h10v10\"></path><path d=\"M7 17 17 7\"></path></svg></div></div></a></div><section class=\"mx-auto mt-16 max-w-2xl\" aria-labelledby=\"faq-heading\"><h2 id=\"faq-heading\" class=\"text-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em]\">FAQ</h2><dl class=\"mt-4 space-y-5\"><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Do the text effects hurt SEO or screen readers?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">No. The real text stays in the DOM as plain characters or with an accessible label, so search engines and screen readers read the words while the animation runs on top.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">How do I install the components in Text?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">With the shadcn CLI. Each component page lists its exact command: free components install from a public URL (npx shadcn add https://useplanes.com/r/&lt;name&gt;.json), Pro components install by name (npx shadcn add @useplanes/&lt;name&gt;) after npx @useplanes/cli init --key &lt;key&gt;.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Do they work with Next.js App Router and Tailwind CSS v4?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Yes. Every component is a React 19 client component styled with Tailwind CSS v4, and works in Next.js App Router, Vite, or any React app with Tailwind CSS v4.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">Are the components in Text free?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">2 of the 9 are free. The rest need a one-time Planes Pro license, which covers every component and future additions.</dd></div><div><dt class=\"text-[0.95rem] font-medium\">What do they depend on?</dt><dd class=\"mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Motion (formerly Framer Motion) is the only runtime animation dependency. The CLI writes the .tsx source into your project, so there is no Planes package to keep updated.</dd></div></dl></section></section>"}